From da1a4f317aec63ca3a0ebdf3514a5585cba523a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:25:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/30] Mana: count every unit of "N mana of any one color"
 when planning payment

Resonating Lute: "Lands you control have '{T}: Add two mana of any one
color. Spend this mana only to cast instant and sorcery spells.'"
CR 106.1 + CR 605.3b: one activation adds all N units at once.

The auto-tap planner listed an "any one color" ability as one row per
color with no combination, so it counted one mana per source. A spell
that needs the extra mana (Divination from two Islands under the Lute)
was never offered as castable, and a player who only taps lands while
paying could not cast it at all. A count above one now gives one atomic
row per color ([U, U], ...), as fixed multi-mana productions already do.
CR 106.6: the spend restriction still filters the rows, so a creature
spell can't use the Lute's mana.

A manual pick of a sacrificial "any one color" source still offers one
choice that asks its color after the cost (CR 605.3b): the per-color
combinations are planner data, so the deferred selection drops them.

Test: tests/integration/any_one_color_multi_mana_castability.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
